  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 - Login",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "auth",
            "login"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          },
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
        },
        "description": {
          "type": "text/markdown",
          "content": "Guarda el `token`.\n\nEl rol importa **dos veces**: decide si el endpoint responde (`role_query`, sin fila = 403) y decide **que filas trae** (el filtro de establecimiento va dentro del SQL). Un `CEVAL-RECTOR` obtiene un archivo mas corto que un `CEVAL-SUPER_ADMINISTRADOR`, con los mismos filtros."
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const d = pm.response.json();",
              "if (d.token) { pm.collectionVariables.set('token', d.token); }"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1 - Sesiones: PDF con los filtros de la pantalla",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/reportes/auditoria-sesiones",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "reportes",
            "auditoria-sesiones"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          },
          "raw": "{\n  \"format\": \"pdf\",\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"AUTHOR\": \"Roberto\",\n    \"STATUS\": \"closed\",\n    \"STARTEDFROM\": \"2026-09-01\",\n    \"STARTEDTO\": \"2026-09-15\"\n  }\n}"
        },
        "description": {
          "content": "La pestana **Por sesion**.\n\n| Filtro | Que hace |\n|---|---|\n| `AUTHOR` | subcadena, sin distinguir mayusculas, sobre el usuario |\n| `STATUS` | `active` o `closed` |\n| `STARTEDFROM` / `STARTEDTO` | rango sobre el inicio de la sesion |\n\nColumnas: Autor, IP, Inicio, Fin, Estado, Operaciones.\n\nUsa **Send and Download** para guardar el archivo.",
          "type": "text/markdown"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('content-type', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/pdf'));",
              "pm.test('attachment', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Disposition')).to.include('attachment'));",
              "pm.test('X-Report-Rows', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Report-Rows')).to.not.be.undefined);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2 - Sesiones: Excel de las SELECCIONADAS",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/reportes/auditoria-sesiones",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "reportes",
            "auditoria-sesiones"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          },
          "raw": "{\n  \"format\": \"excel\",\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"IDS\": \"{{sessionId}}\"\n  }\n}"
        },
        "description": {
          "content": "Las casillas marcadas en la tabla.\n\n`IDS` es una **cadena CSV** de `family_id`, no un array JSON:\n\n```json\n{ \"IDS\": \"abc123,def456\" }\n```\n\nEs el idioma que ya usa V384 para lo mismo (`has(splitByChar(',', :BODY.IDS), ...)`), porque en ClickHouse es la forma natural de recibir una lista por bind.\n\nCuando `IDS` viene, **tiene prioridad**: los demas filtros se ignoran, igual que en `/audits/stats`.",
          "type": "text/markdown"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('content-type', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('spreadsheetml'));",
              "pm.test('attachment', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Disposition')).to.include('attachment'));",
              "pm.test('X-Report-Rows', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Report-Rows')).to.not.be.undefined);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3 - Una TABLA: todos sus cambios (PDF)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/reportes/auditoria-tabla-operaciones",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "reportes",
            "auditoria-tabla-operaciones"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          },
          "raw": "{\n  \"format\": \"pdf\",\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"SLUG\": \"{{tableSlug}}\",\n    \"OCCURREDFROM\": \"2026-09-01\",\n    \"OCCURREDTO\": \"2026-09-15\"\n  }\n}"
        },
        "description": {
          "content": "El detalle al que se entra desde **Por tablas** -> una tabla.\n\n`SLUG` es **obligatorio** y va en el cuerpo, no en la ruta (el listado equivalente si lo lleva en la ruta: `/audit-tables/:SLUG/operations/query`). El reporting-service solo sabe mandar cuerpo, no construir rutas.\n\n**Sin `SLUG` el reporte sale VACIO, no completo.** Es deliberado: ClickHouse no tiene `RAISE`, asi que no se puede fallar con un mensaje desde el SQL, y entre \"cero filas\" y \"el audit_log entero\" la unica opcion segura es cero.\n\nEl slug es el camelCase de la pantalla y se convierte a nombre de tabla dentro de la consulta: `tActaGrado` -> `tacta_grado`, `tSesionWeb` -> `tsesion_web`.\n\nFiltros: `AUTHOR` (busca en usuario **y** en IP), `OPERATIONCH` (`c`/`u`/`d`), `OCCURREDFROM`/`OCCURREDTO`, `IDS` (CSV de `<lsn>-<seq>`).",
          "type": "text/markdown"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('content-type', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/pdf'));",
              "pm.test('attachment', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Disposition')).to.include('attachment'));",
              "pm.test('X-Report-Rows', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Report-Rows')).to.not.be.undefined);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4 - Una tabla: solo los UPDATE (Excel)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/reportes/auditoria-tabla-operaciones",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "reportes",
            "auditoria-tabla-operaciones"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          },
          "raw": "{\n  \"format\": \"excel\",\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"SLUG\": \"{{tableSlug}}\",\n    \"OPERATIONCH\": \"u\"\n  }\n}"
        },
        "description": {
          "content": "`OPERATIONCH` usa la letra de Debezium, no la etiqueta: `c` = INSERT, `u` = UPDATE, `d` = DELETE. La columna exportada si trae la etiqueta legible.",
          "type": "text/markdown"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('content-type', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('spreadsheetml'));",
              "pm.test('attachment', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Disposition')).to.include('attachment'));",
              "pm.test('X-Report-Rows', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Report-Rows')).to.not.be.undefined);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5 - Una SESION: sus cambios (PDF)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/reportes/auditoria-sesion-operaciones",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "reportes",
            "auditoria-sesion-operaciones"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          },
          "raw": "{\n  \"format\": \"pdf\",\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"SESSIONID\": \"{{sessionId}}\"\n  }\n}"
        },
        "description": {
          "content": "La tabla del detalle de una sesion (TABLA / OPERACION / DETALLE / FECHA).\n\n`SESSIONID` es el `family_id` de la sesion, **obligatorio** y por cuerpo, con la misma regla que `SLUG`: sin el, cero filas.\n\nIncluye a proposito las filas de `tsesion_web` (Inicio/Cierre de sesion): es decision de producto desde V380 -- \"Inicio de sesion\" es la primera entrada util de la lista.\n\nFiltros adicionales: `TABLESLUG`, `OPERATIONCH`, `OCCURREDFROM`/`OCCURREDTO`, `IDS`.",
          "type": "text/markdown"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('content-type', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/pdf'));",
              "pm.test('attachment', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Disposition')).to.include('attachment'));",
              "pm.test('X-Report-Rows', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Report-Rows')).to.not.be.undefined);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6 - Sesion: solo una tabla, columnas recortadas",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/reportes/auditoria-sesion-operaciones",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "reportes",
            "auditoria-sesion-operaciones"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          },
          "raw": "{\n  \"format\": \"excel\",\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"SESSIONID\": \"{{sessionId}}\",\n    \"TABLESLUG\": \"academico_test.tgrado\"\n  },\n  \"columns\": [\n    \"occurredAt\",\n    \"operation\",\n    \"entityName\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        "description": {
          "content": "`TABLESLUG` aqui compara contra el valor **tal cual esta guardado** en `audit_log.tabla`, que normalmente lleva el esquema (`academico_test.tgrado`) -- no es el slug camelCase del otro endpoint.\n\n`columns` recorta y reordena; una clave que no este en el catalogo se ignora en silencio.",
          "type": "text/markdown"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('content-type', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('spreadsheetml'));",
              "pm.test('attachment', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Disposition')).to.include('attachment'));",
              "pm.test('X-Report-Rows', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Report-Rows')).to.not.be.undefined);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
